hdef jotx jotx_website

  title jotx
  type page
  description jotx is a block editor for plain-text notes in VS Code, and a one-line script that shows .jot files on any website.

  def menu
    items """Viewer | view.html
GitHub | https://github.com/balaji-embedcentrum/jotx-open"""

  def tab "Home"
    icon 🏠
    def heading "Notes that live in your repo, and read like a web page"
    def paragraph "jotx is a block editor for VS Code. Write with `/` commands, drop in live widgets such as Kanban boards, timelines and decision records, and keep everything as clean, diff-friendly text files next to your code. The same files become web pages with one script tag."
    def badges
      items """version | 3.2.0 | teal
license | Apache-2.0 | slate
VS Code | extension | blue
web | one script tag | violet"""
    def gridcard
      layout 3x2
      def card jnwb1k9x
        title Every block
        icon 🧱
        link "#blocks"
      def card wrq95583
        title 21 live widgets
        icon 🧩
        link "#widgets"
      def card utj3nrkg
        title On the web
        icon 🌐
        link "#web"
    def callout "This website is a single .jot file. Each tab above is a page, and every example on it is a live jotx block. Open it in VS Code with jotx installed to edit any page."
      variant success
    def heading "Start in a minute"
      level 2
    def steps "Getting started"
      steps """[ ] Install jotx | From the VS Code Marketplace, or a .vsix from the GitHub releases
[ ] Create a note | Command Palette → jotx: Create New Note, or make any .jot file
[ ] Type / | Pick a block or widget from the menu; it saves as plain text"""
    def heading "Why plain text"
      level 2
    def columns
      def column
        def heading "In your repo"
          level 3
        def paragraph "Notes sit next to the code they describe. They are reviewed in pull requests, branch with your work, and diff line by line."
      def column
        def heading "Readable without jotx"
          level 3
        def paragraph "A .jot file is indented text with one block per line. You can read it in any editor, grep it, and generate it from scripts."
      def column
        def heading "Made for AI"
          level 3
        def paragraph "Compact syntax uses about 40% fewer tokens than the classic form, so assistants write, read and edit notes cheaply and correctly."

  def tab "Features"
    icon ✨
    def heading "What jotx does"
    def paragraph "An editor that feels like a modern docs page, a file format built for version control, and tools to publish it all."
    def tab "Editor"
      def list
        items """**Slash menu and insert gallery**: type / or use the floating toolbar to add any block or widget
**Page design**: a hero for the opening heading and lead, one aligned column, and an On this page outline
**Tabs**: split a note into pages; tabs inside a tab become a compact card
**Preview mode**: lock a note to read it without accidental edits
**Search**: Cmd/Ctrl+F finds text in every block, including inside closed tabs
**Follows your theme**: light, dark, high contrast and custom VS Code themes"""
    def tab "Files"
      def list
        items """**One file per note**: .jot, with .meet for meetings and .jotx for older notes
**Two syntaxes**: compact (the default for new files) and classic; jotx reads both and converts either way
**Safe saving**: opening and saving a note never changes what it shows
**Attachments**: images and files in an attachments folder next to the note"""
    def tab "Links and graph"
      def list
        items """**Links between notes**: [next](next.jot) opens the note in jotx
**jotx links**: link to another note or to a single block inside it
**Graph view**: the whole workspace, or the notes around the current one
**Cards and buttons**: navigation tiles that open notes, pages or tabs"""
    def tab "AI"
      def paragraph "jotx ships a syntax guide written for AI models, JOTX_FOR_AI.jot. Give it to your assistant and it writes valid notes with tables, diagrams and widgets. Compact syntax keeps the files short, and jotx validate checks the result."
      def terminal "Check what an assistant wrote"
        shell zsh
        commands """$ npx @jotx-labs/cli validate plan.jot
✅ plan.jot is valid!"""
    def tab "Export"
      def table export "Getting notes out"
        columns Format, How
        rows """Markdown | jotx: Export to Markdown, or jotx convert in the CLI
Word and PDF | The export menu in the editor
HTML page | jotx convert notes.jot -o notes.html
Website | jotx site build"""

  def tab "Blocks"
    icon 🧱
    def heading "Every block"
    def paragraph "Blocks are the building pieces of a note. Each one is a def line in the file; the quoted value is its main text or title."
    def tab "Text"
      def heading "Headings and paragraphs"
        level 2
      def paragraph "Paragraphs take **bold**, *italic*, ~~strike~~, ==highlight==, `code` and [links](https://github.com/balaji-embedcentrum/jotx-open)."
      def code
        language jotx
        text """def heading "Goals"
  level 2

def paragraph "Text with **bold**, `code` and [links](https://jotx.dev).""""
      def heading "Lists and checklists"
        level 2
      def columns
        def column
          def list
            items """Write the plan
Review it
Ship it"""
        def column
          def checklist
            items """[x] Security review
[ ] Launch post"""
