      def paragraph "Indent a menu line with two spaces to put it in the dropdown of the line above. A table of contents lists the headings of the note."

  def tab "Syntax"
    icon 📝
    def heading "The .jot format"
    def paragraph "A .jot file is a header and then blocks, one def line each. Indentation is two spaces; properties and child blocks sit under their block."
    def code
      language jotx
      text """"hdef jotx release_plan

  title Release plan
  type page

  def heading "Shipping 3.2"

  def paragraph "Plain text with **bold** and `code`."

  def checklist
    items """[x] Tabs
[ ] Launch post"""""""
    def table rules "Rules"
      columns Rule, Example
      rows """Two spaces of indentation | properties and children under their def line
The quoted value is the main text or title | def heading "Goals"
One property per line | language bash
Multi-line values go in triple quotes | items followed by three quotes
Ids only where something links to the block | def table risks "Risks"
Leave out defaults | heading level 1, list bulleted, chart bar"""
    def heading "Compact and classic"
      level 2
    def paragraph "Compact is the default for new files and uses about 40% fewer tokens. Classic puts every value on its own line and gives every block an id. jotx reads both; convert a file or the whole workspace from the Command Palette, or with the CLI."
    def terminal "Convert"
      shell zsh
      commands """$ jotx migrate notes/ --to compact
12 of 12 files converted to compact syntax (38% smaller)."""
    def heading "For AI assistants"
      level 2
    def paragraph "JOTX_FOR_AI.jot is the complete syntax reference in a form models follow well. It ships with the extension (jotx: Open Help Files)."

  def tab "VS Code"
    icon 💻
    def heading "jotx in VS Code"
    def paragraph "Every .jot file opens in the jotx editor. Right-click a file and choose Open With → Text Editor to edit the text directly, with syntax highlighting, completions and hover help."
    def table commands "Commands"
      columns Command, What it does
      rows """jotx: Create New Note | A new .jot file from a template
jotx: Open Help Files | The guides, examples and templates
Show Graph View | Every note and link in the workspace
Show Local Graph | The notes around the current one
jotx: Export to Markdown | Save the note as Markdown
jotx: Import from Markdown | Turn a Markdown file into a note
Convert Workspace Syntax… | Rewrite every note in compact or classic syntax
Show Output Logs | The jotx output channel, for troubleshooting"""
    def table settings "Settings"
      columns Setting, Default, Meaning
      rows """jotx.syntax | preserve | The syntax jotx writes when it saves: preserve, compact or classic
jotx.spellCheck.enabled | false | Spell checking in the editor
jotx.nodeManager.excludeFolders | jotx-help, node_modules, .git | Folders left out of the graph and links"""
    def shortcuts "Keyboard"
      items """/ | Block and widget menu
Cmd+B | Bold
Cmd+I | Italic
Cmd+F | Search the note, including closed tabs
Cmd+Z | Undo
Cmd+Shift+Z | Redo"""

  def tab "Web"
    icon 🌐
    def heading "jotx on the web"
    def paragraph "Show one note on any page with a script tag, or publish a folder of notes as a complete website."
    def tab "Embed a note"
      def code
        language html
        text """<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@jotx-labs/embed@3.2.0/dist/jotx.min.js"></script>

<jotx-doc src="notes/launch-plan.jot"></jotx-doc>"""
      def table attributes "Attributes"
        columns Attribute, Meaning
        rows """src | The .jot file to show, relative to the page
theme | auto (the default), light or dark
outline | Show the On this page rail beside wide pages"""
      def paragraph "Documents render read-only and follow the reader's light or dark setting. Mermaid, Chart.js and KaTeX load only when a document uses them. A .jot file is data with no code inside, so showing one on your site cannot run anything."
    def tab "One-file sites"
      def paragraph "A note that starts with tabs is a whole website: the tabs become its top navigation, a tab that holds tabs gets a dropdown, and a menu block just before the tabs adds its links on the right. This page is one."
      def code
        language jotx
        text """def menu
  items "GitHub | https://github.com/example"

def tab "Home"
  def heading "My product"
def tab "Docs"
  def heading "Documentation"
  def tab "Install"
    def paragraph "..."
  def tab "Configure"
    def paragraph "...""""
      def paragraph "Link to a page with its name: #docs, or #install for a page inside Docs. On narrow screens the navigation folds into a Menu button."
    def tab "Publish a site"
      def paragraph "jotx site build turns a folder of .jot files into a static website: a page for every file at a clean address, a menu, folder and tag pages, an RSS feed, a sitemap and search. Dated posts appear on the home page as cards."
      def terminal "Build and preview"
        shell zsh
        commands """$ jotx site serve notes/
Preview at http://localhost:4000, reloads on save
$ jotx site build notes/
✅ Built 24 pages and a search index in notes/_site"""
      def filetree "A site"
        tree """notes/
  site.jot  // title, address, menu, footer
  index.jot  // home page
  guides/start.jot  // /guides/start/
  blog/first-post.jot  // dated, tagged post
  attachments/logo.svg"""
      def paragraph "The output is plain files: upload them to GitHub Pages, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages or any web server. No Node.js is needed on the server."
    def tab "CLI"
      def table cli "jotx command line"
        columns Command, What it does
        rows """jotx validate notes.jot | Check a file; exits with 1 on errors
jotx migrate notes/ --to compact | Convert files to compact or classic syntax
jotx convert notes.jot -o notes.html | One self-contained HTML page
jotx site build notes/ | Build a website into _site
jotx site serve notes/ | Preview with live reload
jotx parse notes.jot | The syntax tree as JSON"""
      def code
        language bash
        text npm install -g @jotx-labs/cli

