[jotx for AI](view.html?src=examples/JOTX_FOR_AI.jot): the syntax reference for assistants"""

  def tab "FAQ"
    icon ❓
    def heading "Questions"
    def tab "Using jotx"
      def toggle "Do I need VS Code?"
        def paragraph "To edit visually, yes. A .jot file is plain text, so any editor can open it, and the web script and CLI work without VS Code."
      def toggle "Can I still use Markdown?"
        def paragraph "Import a Markdown file with jotx: Import from Markdown, and export any note back to Markdown."
      def toggle "Where are images stored?"
        def paragraph "In an attachments folder next to the note. Paste or drop an image into the editor and jotx saves it there."
      def toggle "Will saving change my file?"
        def paragraph "Only what you edit. Opening and saving a note keeps everything it shows, and jotx keeps the syntax you chose (see the jotx.syntax setting)."
    def tab "On the web"
      def toggle "Does my web server need Node.js?"
        def paragraph "No. jotx site build writes plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript files. Any web server or static host can serve them."
      def toggle "Why does a page not open when I double-click the HTML file?"
        def paragraph "Browsers do not let a page opened from disk read other files next to it. Preview with jotx site serve, or publish the folder to a host such as GitHub Pages."
      def toggle "Is it safe to show .jot files from others?"
        def paragraph "Yes. A .jot file is data: the web script renders it read-only, escapes all text and only follows web and relative links."
    def tab "Project"
      def toggle "What does jotx cost?"
        def paragraph "Nothing. jotx is open source under the Apache-2.0 licence."
      def toggle "How do I report a bug or ask for a feature?"
        def paragraph "Open an issue on GitHub. Security issues go through GitHub's private vulnerability reporting."
      def button 24nug85r
        label jotx on GitHub
        link https://github.com/balaji-embedcentrum/jotx-open
